Z||000000||Wolfhound||11-25-1999||08:02 AM||||Has anyone changed out the entire frontend assembly (suspension and steering) on a pre 88 car as a unit? Is it as straight forward as it appears.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 11-26-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||pollock||11-30-1999||06:07 PM||||I rebuilt mine this weekend.  What exactly do you mean by "change out"?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||11-30-1999||06:47 PM||||Can you remove the entire front suspension from the same model intact. I have just found a good running 86 SE Tech 4 5 speed, with a damaged front suspension. I have another that is in good condition on a parts car. My question is can it be swapped as a unit without disassembling the coil springs etc?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||11-30-1999||09:41 PM||||I believe that it can. I seem to remember seeing a number of them laying around at Ed Parks' place.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||11-30-1999||10:05 PM||||Yes, the whole front suspension assembly will unbolt and drop out. Of course, you have to disconnect the steering column coupler at the rack first. ONCE you've broken the rusty old bolts loose, it's not all that tough if you have two people working. I believe all non-88 front ends are interchangeable. I've heard conflicting stories about installing an 88 unit into earlier Fieros. No reason to put an older one into an 88.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wolfhound||12-01-1999||03:55 AM||||Thanks, guys thats what I needed to know. Raydar, the Car is in Huntsville about 225 miles north of here. I have a well equiped shop to use there and I,ll be going to Toney Ala. to Ed Parks Fiero Factory while I,m there. That,s something I,ve just got to see.<BR>Coy||||reg||1
